  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Have got** = tener (inglés británico).",
      "",
      "| Sujeto | Afirmativa | Negativa |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| I / you / we / they | have got (I've got) | haven't got |",
      "| he / she / it | has got (she's got) | hasn't got |",
      "",
      "**Pregunta:** *Have you got…? Has she got…?* **Respuesta:** *Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.*",
      "",
      "En inglés americano se usa más *I have* y *Do you have…?*; ambas formas se entienden. *'s got* = *has got*, no *is*."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "She have got two sisters.",
        "right": "She has got two sisters. / She's got two sisters.",
        "note": "Con he/she/it se usa has."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "Yes, I've.",
        "right": "Yes, I have.",
        "note": "En la respuesta corta afirmativa no se contrae."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
